\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Come, O Thou traveller unknown,
\par Whom still I hold, but cannot see!
\par My company before is gone,
\par And I am left alone with Thee;
\par WIth Thee all night I mean to stay,
\par And wrestle till the break of day.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. I need not tell Thee who I am,
\par My misery and sin declare;
\par Thyself hast called me by my name;
\par Look on Thy hands, and read it there:
\par But who, I ask Thee, who art Thou?
\par Tell me Thy name, and tell me now.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. In vain Thou strugglest to get free;
\par I never will unloose my hold!
\par Art Thou the Man that died for me?
\par The secret of Thy love unfold:
\par Wrestling, I will not let Thee go,
\par Till I Thy name, Thy nature know.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Wilt Thou not yet to me reveal
\par Thy new, unutterable name?
\par Tell me, I still beseech Thee, tell;
\par To know it now resolved I am:
\par Wrestling, I will not let Thee go,
\par Till I Thy name, Thy nature know.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. What though my shrinking flesh complain,
\par And murmur to contend so long?
\par I rise superior to my pain,
\par When I am weak, then I am strong;
\par And when my all of strength shall fail,
\par I shall with the God-Man prevail.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Yield to me now; for I am weak,
\par But confident in self-despair;
\par Speak to my heart, in blessings speak,
\par Be conquered by my instant prayer;
\par Speak, or Thou never hence shalt move,
\par And tell me if Thy name is Love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. 'Tis Love! 'tis Love! Thou diedst for me!
\par I hear Thy whisper in my heart;
\par The morning breaks, the shadows flee,
\par Pure, universal Love Thou art;
\par To me, to all, Thy mercies move;
\par Thy nature and Thy name is Love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. My prayer hath power with God; the grace
\par Unspeakable I now receive;
\par Through faith I see Thee face to face, 
\par I see Thee face to face, and live!
\par In vain I have not wept and strove:
\par Thy nature and Thy name is Love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 9\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 9. I know Thee, Saviour, who Thou art,
\par Jesus, the feeble sinner's Friend;
\par Nor wilt Thou with the night depart,
\par But stay and love me to the end;
\par Thy mercies never shall remove:
\par Thy nature and Thy name is Love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 10\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 10. The Sun of Righteousness on me
\par Hath risen with healing in His wings;
\par Withered my nature's strength,  from Thee
\par My soul its life and succour brings;
\par My help is all laid up above:
\par Thy nature and Thy name is Love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 11\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 11. Contented now upon my thigh
\par I halt, till life's short journey end;
\par All helplessness, all weakness, I
\par On Thee alone for strength depend;
\par Nor have I power from Thee to move:
\par Thy nature and Thy name is Love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 12\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 12. Lame as I am, I take the prey,
\par Hell, earth, and sin with ease o'ercome;
\par I leap for joy, pursue my way,
\par And as a bounding hart fly home,
\par Through all eternity to prove
\par Thy nature and Thy name is Love.
\par \f1 
